Staff involved in the operating of ionising equipment shall undergo medical examinations. Full medical examination and a full blood examination to be conducted by a registered medical practitioner;
Pre-employment medical examination; 
Regular medical examination (at least once in three years and more frequent for those exposed to higher ionizing radiation)
Termination/completion of services.

Specific performance indicators (among others) are tracked e.g.;
Workload indicator summary for different imaging modalities.
Number of rejected films (reject rate).
